docs/agents/generated/wiki_publisher.md:3:Generic, tracker- and wiki-agnostic base agent that turns a work item's prepared context into one wiki page: it reads the input bundle (`input/<KEY>/`), writes the page as GitHub-flavored Markdown to `outputs/response.md`, and the post-action syncs it to the wiki (Confluence via the dmtools Markdown sync today) and posts the page link back to the originating ticket on Jira, Azure DevOps, or GitHub Issues.
docs/agents/generated/story_acceptance_criteria.md:3:Generates structured, testable Acceptance Criteria for a Story from `input/` context (description, designs, and answered question sub-tickets), enforcing `acceptance_criteria_quality.md` and replacing the ticket's `Acceptance Criteria` field (or syncing to Confluence when configured), then advancing the story via `assignForSolutionArchitecture.js`.
docs/agents/generated/story_description.md:3:Writes an enhanced Story `Description` from `input/` context and answered `existing_questions.json` sub-tickets while preserving all original attachment and link references (`preserve_references.md`), then assigns the ticket back for review.
